        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): generate gateway protocol models",
        "body": "Closes #105960\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAndroid hand-maintains gateway frame models, protocol versions, method names, event names, capabilities, and command constants. That surface can drift from the canonical TypeBox protocol and from the generated Swift client.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a Kotlin generator that reads the canonical gateway schemas, core method descriptors, and event coverage source, then emits the Android models and catalogs the app currently consumes. Android keeps its existing kotlinx.serialization stack and shipped structured-params compatibility; a package script provides generated-file drift checks without introducing a second hand-maintained path.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo direct UI change. Android protocol updates now follow the canonical gateway definitions instead of requiring manual model and constant edits.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxctak5a5mkg0p7g3tqp7xwm`: Kotlin generation was byte-for-byte deterministic after regeneration.\n- `pnpm android:lint`\n- `./gradlew :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.gateway.GatewayProtocolGeneratedTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.protocol.OpenClawProtocolConstantsTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.gateway.GatewaySessionInvokeTest`\n- Fresh autoreview: no accepted or actionable findings.\n- `pnpm check:changed` reached the repository TypeScript LOC ratchet, then stopped on unrelated stale baseline entries outside this PR's eight files.\n",
